title: The Workers' Militias
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and c_militias_timer <= 0 and time >= 3
on-arrival: {!
Q.c_militias_timer = 4;
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.c_arms_ok = 0;
!}
frequency: 200
is-card: true
tags: movement

= The Workers' Militias

[? if year <= 1920 : Rifles from the army depots of November are still hidden in allotment sheds and cellars, and the Freikorps are better armed every month. ?][? if year = 1921 : Under the disarmament laws the police search the workers' districts for weapons, while the civil guards of the propertied keep theirs. ?][? if year >= 1922 : Works councils in many towns have formed proletarian hundreds, communists and social democrats together, to defend meetings against the nationalist leagues. [? if year >= 1923 : Prussia has banned them. In Saxony and Thuringia they drill openly. ?] ?]

Our armed men are few, and they listen to their own commanders as much as to the Zentrale. A Reichswehr quartermaster in Spandau has let it be known that he has rifles to sell.

- @quartermaster: Buy his rifles.
- @control: Put every unit under the Zentrale's command.
- @joint: Form joint units with the social democratic workers.
- @disarm: Stand them down.
- @easy_discard

@quartermaster
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. The Spandau comrades think he is probably honest.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
if (Math.random() < 0.65) {
    Q.c_arms_ok = 1;
    Q.red_guards_arms += 10;
} else {
    Q.c_arms_ok = 2;
    Q.repression += 8;
    Q.red_guards_strength = Math.max(0, Q.red_guards_strength - 0.3);
    RG.news('Communists arrested buying army rifles in Spandau');
}
!}

[? if c_arms_ok = 1 : He is a sergeant with debts and a brother in the USPD. The crates arrive on time. ?][? if c_arms_ok = 2 : He was working for the police. Three comrades are arrested at the handover, and the money is gone. ?]

@control
subtitle: The militias obey the Zentrale. Their local commanders resent it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.red_guards_loyalty += 12;
if (!Q.ultraleft_gone) {
    Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 5;
}
!}

Every unit now has a political commissar named by the district, and every district answers to Berlin.

@joint
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Far more men, and far less say over them.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any deal with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.red_guards_strength += 2;
Q.red_guards_loyalty -= 8;
Q.spd_relation += 3;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

Every big works elects its own unit at a factory meeting. They argue about everything except who the enemy is.

@disarm
subtitle: Fewer armed men and fewer raids. The Left is furious.
on-arrival: {!
Q.repression -= 6;
Q.red_guards_strength *= 0.7;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 6;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

A rifle in the cellar is an invitation to the Freikorps, the Zentrale argues. Not every unit obeys.
